<article class="env-lemma" id="CE7D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/CE7D">Lemma <span data-tag="CE7D">5.5.3.15</span>.</a> Let $p: \calM \rightarrow \Delta ^1$ be a Cartesian fibration, let $\calC $ denote the $\infty $-category of sections of $p$, and let $e: X \rightarrow Y$ and $e': X' \rightarrow Y'$ be objects of $\calC $. If $e'$ is $p$-Cartesian, then the evaluation map $\bHom _{\calC }( e,e') \rightarrow \bHom _{\calM }(Y,Y')$ is a homotopy equivalence. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      There is a homotopy pullback diagram of simplicial sets, whose image in the homotopy category $\calH $ is isomorphic to 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \bHom _{\calC }(e,e') \ar [r] \ar [d] &  \bHom _{\calM }(Y,Y') \ar [d] \\ \bHom _{\calM }(X,X') \ar [r] &  \bHom _{\calM }(X,Y'). } \]
</div>
    <p>
       If $e'$ is $p$-Cartesian, then the lower horizonal map is a homotopy equivalence, so the upper horizonal map is a homotopy equivalence as well. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>